   "subject": "Random effects in inlabru",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all, I&#39;m making a predicted distribution of fig trees in a landscape (as a point process), and trying to incorporate different land-uses as a random effect.<div><br></div><div>However I think my wording isn&#39;t right for inlabru- heres the full model, with the random effect line specified.</div><div><br></div><span style=\"font-size:small\">## Define SPDE</span><br style=\"font-size:small\"><span style=\"font-size:small\">Fig_SPDE &lt;- inla.spde2.pcmatern(mesh, alpha = 2, prior.range = c(150, 0.01), prior.sigma = c(2, 0.05))</span><br style=\"font-size:small\"><span style=\"font-size:small\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size:small\"><u>## Here are my covariates, with random effects specific in <b>bold</b>.</u></span><br style=\"font-size:small\"><span style=\"font-size:small\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size:small\">Fig_cmp &lt;- coordinates ~ Fig_GRF(map = coordinates, model = Fig_SPDE) + Intercept +  <b>Mixed_cov(f(map= Mixed_SPDF, model = &quot;iid&quot;, const=T)) + Mono_cov(f(map= Mono_SPDF, model = &quot;iid&quot;</b></span><b style=\"font-size:small\">, const=T</b><b style=\"font-size:small\">))</b><span style=\"font-size:small\"> + Elev_cov(map = Elev_SPDF, model = &quot;linear&quot;) + ACD_cov(map = ACD_SPDF, model = &quot;linear&quot;) + FigRivers_cov(map = Rivers_SPDF, model = &quot;linear&quot;)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(80,0,80);font-size:small\">Error in match.names(clabs, names(xi)) :</span></div><span style=\"color:rgb(80,0,80);font-size:small\">  names do not match previous names</span><div><br></div><div><b>This is the error I&#39;m getting consistently^</b></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small\"><br></span></div><div><div><span style=\"font-size:small\">Does anyone have any suggestions? </span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small\">Thanks for your help!</span></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Kivlj2A3AQAJ",
   "from": "Finn Lindgren",
   "author": "afb003e064114795",
   "date": "2020-05-22T11:34:51Z",
   "subject": "Re: [r-inla] Random effects in inlabru",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\">Remove the f() notation; the name(map=...) syntax is instead of f() for random effects, not in addition to.<br><br><div dir=\"ltr\">Finn</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><blockquote type=\"cite\">On 22 May 2020, at 12:32, S Milne &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sm0...@my.bristol.ac.uk</a>&gt; wrote:<br><br></blockquote></div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\">﻿</div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all, I&#39;m making a predicted distribution of fig trees in a landscape (as a point process), and trying to incorporate different land-uses as a random effect.<div><br></div><div>However I think my wording isn&#39;t right for inlabru- heres the full model, with the random effect line specified.</div><div><br></div><span style=\"font-size:small\">## Define SPDE</span><br style=\"font-size:small\"><span style=\"font-size:small\">Fig_SPDE &lt;- inla.spde2.pcmatern(mesh, alpha = 2, prior.range = c(150, 0.01), prior.sigma = c(2, 0.05))</span><br style=\"font-size:small\"><span style=\"font-size:small\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size:small\"><u>## Here are my covariates, with random effects specific in <b>bold</b>.</u></span><br style=\"font-size:small\"><span style=\"font-size:small\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size:small\">Fig_cmp &lt;- coordinates ~ Fig_GRF(map = coordinates, model = Fig_SPDE) + Intercept +  <b>Mixed_cov(f(map= Mixed_SPDF, model = &quot;iid&quot;, const=T)) + Mono_cov(f(map= Mono_SPDF, model = &quot;iid&quot;</b></span><b style=\"font-size:small\">, const=T</b><b style=\"font-size:small\">))</b><span style=\"font-size:small\"> + Elev_cov(map = Elev_SPDF, model = &quot;linear&quot;) + ACD_cov(map = ACD_SPDF, model = &quot;linear&quot;) + FigRivers_cov(map = Rivers_SPDF, model = &quot;linear&quot;)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(80,0,80);font-size:small\">Error in match.names(clabs, names(xi)) :</span></div><span style=\"color:rgb(80,0,80);font-size:small\">  names do not match previous names</span><div><br></div><div><b>This is the error I&#39;m getting consistently^</b></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small\"><br></span></div><div><div><span style=\"font-size:small\">Does anyone have any suggestions? </span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small\">Thanks for your help!</span></div></div></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
