   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi,\r<br>\r<br>I&#39;d need to see the exact code that gives the error, and the\r<br>traceback() output to have any chance of debugging that, since it\r<br>doesn&#39;t seem to be at all the same as the previous problem in the\r<br>thread (the spurious f() calls), and there are no calls to\r<br>match.names() in the inlabru code.\r<br>\r<br>But yes, the tutorial was initially written for an earlier version\r<br>where the direct use of a SpatialPixelsDataFrame object instead of an\r<br>&quot;f.extract.covariate()&quot; function call hadn&#39;t been implemented. If I\r<br>recall correctly, the second half of the tutorial does use that new\r<br>functionality, but gives an incorrect reason for why. The\r<br>f.evel()-like code is now part of the package, and the user only needs\r<br>to make their own if the built-in version can&#39;t do the right thing,\r<br>for whatever reason.\r<br>\r<br>Do make sure to check this on the github devel branch version, since\r<br>there are some bug fixes there that are not on CRAN. Soon there will\r<br>also be an entirely new version that should clear up most of these\r<br>issues.\r<br>\r<br>Finn\r<br>"
    ],
