     3,
     "\r<br>On Sat, 18 Jul 2020 at 00:33, Matt Williamson\r<br>&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mattwill...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Hello,\r<br>&gt; Can you clarify the appropriate syntax for continuous covariates? Your response seems to suggest that the following is correct:\r<br>&gt; model &lt;- coordinates ~ continuous.cov(map = continuous.cov.spdf, model=&quot;linear&quot;)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; however, the tutorial on <a href=\"http://inlabru.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://inlabru.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440661885000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ajbUNW4MU8JnnOOzYBmNQ\">inlabru.org</a> suggests this is necessary:\r<br>&gt; f.elev &lt;- function(x,y) {\r<br>&gt;   # turn coordinates into SpatialPoints object:\r<br>&gt;   spp &lt;- SpatialPoints(data.frame(x=x,y=y))\r<br>&gt;   # attach the appropriate coordinate reference system (CRS)\r<br>&gt;   proj4string(spp) &lt;- CRS(proj4string(elev))\r<br>&gt;   # Extract elevation values at spp coords, from our elev SpatialGridDataFrame\r<br>&gt;   v &lt;- over(spp, elev)\r<br>&gt;   v[<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440661885000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3-6LemBfOPmdVCJfuLFMGk\">is.na</a>(v)] &lt;- 0 # NAs are a problem! Remove them\r<br>&gt;   return(v$elevation)\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; emdl &lt;- coordinates ~ beta.elev(map = f.elev(x,y), model = &quot;linear&quot;)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; However, when I try the latter with a different covariate (named `roughness`), I get the error mentioned above:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Error in match.names(clabs, names(xi)) :\r<br>&gt;   names do not match previous names\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Has the syntax changed since the tutorial was written? Or can you point me to which &#39;names&#39; are mismatching when this error is thrown?\r<br>&gt; Thank you,\r<br>&gt; M\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; On Friday, May 22, 2020 at 5:34:51 AM UTC-6, Finn Lindgren wrote:\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; Remove the f() notation; the name(map=...) syntax is instead of f() for random effects, not in addition to.\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; Finn\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; On 22 May 2020, at 12:32, S Milne &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sm0...@my.bristol.ac.uk</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; ﻿\r<br>&gt;&gt; Hi all, I&#39;m making a predicted distribution of fig trees in a landscape (as a point process), and trying to incorporate different land-uses as a random effect.\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; However I think my wording isn&#39;t right for inlabru- heres the full model, with the random effect line specified.\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; ## Define SPDE\r<br>&gt;&gt; Fig_SPDE &lt;- inla.spde2.pcmatern(mesh, alpha = 2, prior.range = c(150, 0.01), prior.sigma = c(2, 0.05))\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; ## Here are my covariates, with random effects specific in bold.\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; Fig_cmp &lt;- coordinates ~ Fig_GRF(map = coordinates, model = Fig_SPDE) + Intercept +  Mixed_cov(f(map= Mixed_SPDF, model = &quot;iid&quot;, const=T)) + Mono_cov(f(map= Mono_SPDF, model = &quot;iid&quot;, const=T)) + Elev_cov(map = Elev_SPDF, model = &quot;linear&quot;) + ACD_cov(map = ACD_SPDF, model = &quot;linear&quot;) + FigRivers_cov(map = Rivers_SPDF, model = &quot;linear&quot;)\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;Error in match.names(clabs, names(xi)) :\r<br>&gt;&gt;   names do not match previous names\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; This is the error I&#39;m getting consistently^\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; Does anyone have any suggestions?\r<br>&gt;&gt; Thanks for your help!\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; --\r<br>&gt;&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;R-inla discussion group&quot; group.\r<br>"
